The first horizontal-whitespace token on a line has a width-dependent,
usually positive response. Opening a code block weakens it; numbered source
listings strengthen it. Blank lines and document starts also weaken it. Later
whitespace has little effect. An initial token 'Title' is negative; if the
next token is ':', that colon is strongly positive. Other text predicts zero.
