The negative family centres on storm/worm and short rhotic fragments such
as orm, urm, org and orph. The positive family includes Cyrillic ш/щ
continuations (especially after о), orth/forth, and phosphoryl spellings.
Word continuation and the immediately preceding letters change the size.
A repeated middle-dot leader has a small positive response.
Most other tokens receive zero. This is a lexical approximation, not a
claim that these fragments share a meaning.
