"""Approximate a negative signal for newly starting zeroes and o-like fragments.

A zero inside a number is quiet; a zero after a date/grouping separator is
stronger. Short o-like pieces respond at word boundaries, whereas familiar
complete words and letter continuations are mostly quiet. Cyrillic/Greek o
and Japanese/Korean o syllables are included. Repeated middle-dot leaders
have a separate positive response. All context is limited to this document.
