"""A sparse byte/formatting and digit-5 detector, with a start-of-text bias.

NUL padding has a negative response depending on the preceding character.
Carriage-return prefixes and long, CR-dominated runs are positive. Digit 5 is
positive after letters, especially in MD5, HTML5 and HDF5. Selected
spellings of five and fifteen also respond. Repeated middle dots are
negative. At document starts, case, spacing, comment markers and the
label 'Title:' matter.
This deliberately omits the many small word-specific responses.
