"""A sparse, spelling-sensitive lock/kn response.

Lock inflections and identifiers are strongly negative, unlike block/clock/flock.
The root can straddle tokens.  Chinese lock characters and Japanese ロック
also give negative values.  Smaller rules cover kn/knock fragments and positive
lain/l+ain spellings.  This deliberately leaves other rare responses unexplained.
State is just the current word fragment and previous token, reset per document.
